---The metadata for a file. Some resource methods (such as `files.update`) require a `fileId`. Use the `files.list` method to retrieve the ID for a file.
---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.File
---@field canReadRevisions? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `capabilities/canReadRevisions` instead.
---@field sharingUser? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.User Output only. User that shared the item with the current user, if available.
---@field labelInfo? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileLabelInfo Output only. An overview of the labels on the file.
---@field alternateLink? string Output only. A link for opening the file in a relevant Google editor or viewer.
---@field sha256Checksum? string Output only. The SHA256 checksum associated with this file, if available. This field is only populated for files with content stored in Google Drive; it is not populated for Docs Editors or shortcut files.
---@field shared? boolean Output only. Whether the file has been shared. Not populated for items in shared drives.
---@field capabilities? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileCapabilities Output only. Capabilities the current user has on this file. Each capability corresponds to a fine-grained action that a user may take.
---@field editable? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `capabilities/canEdit` instead.
---@field owners? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UserList Output only. The owner of this file. Only certain legacy files may have more than one owner. This field isn't populated for items in shared drives.
---@field videoMediaMetadata? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileVideoMediaMetadata Output only. Metadata about video media. This will only be present for video types.
---@field ownerNames? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringList Output only. Name(s) of the owner(s) of this file. Not populated for items in shared drives.
---@field originalFilename? string The original filename of the uploaded content if available, or else the original value of the `title` field. This is only available for files with binary content in Google Drive.
---@field title? string The title of this file. Note that for immutable items such as the top level folders of shared drives, My Drive root folder, and Application Data folder the title is constant.
---@field exportLinks? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringMap Output only. Links for exporting Docs Editors files to specific formats.
---@field kind? string Output only. The type of file. This is always `drive#file`.
---@field description? string A short description of the file.
---@field sharedWithMeDate? string Time at which this file was shared with the user (formatted RFC 3339 timestamp).
---@field indexableText? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileIndexableText Indexable text attributes for the file (can only be written)
---@field createdDate? string Create time for this file (formatted RFC 3339 timestamp).
---@field copyRequiresWriterPermission? boolean Whether the options to copy, print, or download this file, should be disabled for readers and commenters.
---@field defaultOpenWithLink? string Output only. A link to open this file with the user's default app for this file. Only populated when the drive.apps.readonly scope is used.
---@field inheritedPermissionsDisabled? boolean Whether this file has inherited permissions disabled. Inherited permissions are enabled by default.
---@field md5Checksum? string Output only. An MD5 checksum for the content of this file. This field is only populated for files with content stored in Google Drive; it is not populated for Docs Editors or shortcut files.
---@field openWithLinks? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringMap Output only. A map of the id of each of the user's apps to a link to open this file with that app. Only populated when the drive.apps.readonly scope is used.
---@field canComment? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `capabilities/canComment` instead.
---@field modifiedDate? string Last time this file was modified by anyone (formatted RFC 3339 timestamp). This is only mutable on update when the setModifiedDate parameter is set.
---@field writersCanShare? boolean Whether writers can share the document with other users. Not populated for items in shared drives.
---@field fileSize? string Output only. Size in bytes of blobs and first party editor files. Won't be populated for files that have no size, like shortcuts and folders.
---@field thumbnailVersion? string Output only. The thumbnail version for use in thumbnail cache invalidation.
---@field lastModifyingUser? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.User Output only. The last user to modify this file. This field is only populated when the last modification was performed by a signed-in user.
---@field webViewLink? string Output only. A link only available on public folders for viewing their static web assets (HTML, CSS, JS, etc) via Google Drive's Website Hosting.
---@field fileExtension? string Output only. The final component of `fullFileExtension` with trailing text that does not appear to be part of the extension removed. This field is only populated for files with content stored in Google Drive; it is not populated for Docs Editors or shortcut files.
---@field trashedDate? string The time that the item was trashed (formatted RFC 3339 timestamp). Only populated for items in shared drives.
---@field driveId? string Output only. ID of the shared drive the file resides in. Only populated for items in shared drives.
---@field shortcutDetails? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileShortcutDetails Shortcut file details. Only populated for shortcut files, which have the mimeType field set to `application/vnd.google-apps.shortcut`. Can only be set on `files.insert` requests.
---@field permissionIds? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringList Output only. List of permission IDs for users with access to this file.
---@field ownedByMe? boolean Output only. Whether the file is owned by the current user. Not populated for items in shared drives.
---@field teamDriveId? string Output only. Deprecated: Use `driveId` instead.
---@field folderColorRgb? string Folder color as an RGB hex string if the file is a folder or a shortcut to a folder. The list of supported colors is available in the folderColorPalette field of the About resource. If an unsupported color is specified, it will be changed to the closest color in the palette.
---@field resourceKey? string Output only. A key needed to access the item via a shared link.
---@field fullFileExtension? string Output only. The full file extension; extracted from the title. May contain multiple concatenated extensions, such as "tar.gz". Removing an extension from the title does not clear this field; however, changing the extension on the title does update this field. This field is only populated for files with content stored in Google Drive; it is not populated for Docs Editors or shortcut files.
---@field clientEncryptionDetails? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.ClientEncryptionDetails Client Side Encryption related details. Contains details about the encryption state of the file and details regarding the encryption mechanism that clients need to use when decrypting the contents of this item. This will only be present on files and not on folders or shortcuts.
---@field version? string Output only. A monotonically increasing version number for the file. This reflects every change made to the file on the server, even those not visible to the requesting user.
---@field contentRestrictions? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.ContentRestrictionList Restrictions for accessing the content of the file. Only populated if such a restriction exists.
---@field imageMediaMetadata? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileImageMediaMetadata Output only. Metadata about image media. This will only be present for image types, and its contents will depend on what can be parsed from the image content.
---@field webContentLink? string Output only. A link for downloading the content of the file in a browser using cookie based authentication. In cases where the content is shared publicly, the content can be downloaded without any credentials.
---@field isAppAuthorized? boolean Output only. Whether the file was created or opened by the requesting app.
---@field trashingUser? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.User Output only. If the file has been explicitly trashed, the user who trashed it. Only populated for items in shared drives.
---@field properties? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PropertyList_ The list of properties.
---@field spaces? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringList Output only. The list of spaces which contain the file. Supported values are `drive`, `appDataFolder` and `photos`.
---@field linkShareMetadata? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileLinkShareMetadata Contains details about the link URLs that clients are using to refer to this item.
---@field iconLink? string Output only. A link to the file's icon.
---@field thumbnail? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileThumbnail A thumbnail for the file. This will only be used if a standard thumbnail cannot be generated.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. A link back to this file.
---@field copyable? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `capabilities/canCopy` instead.
---@field id? string The ID of the file.
---@field appDataContents? boolean Output only. Whether this file is in the Application Data folder.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileLabels A group of labels for the file.
---@field permissions? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PermissionList_ Output only. The list of permissions for users with access to this file. Not populated for items in shared drives.
---@field lastModifyingUserName? string Output only. Name of the last user to modify this file.
---@field lastViewedByMeDate? string Last time this file was viewed by the user (formatted RFC 3339 timestamp).
---@field markedViewedByMeDate? string Deprecated.
---@field mimeType? string The MIME type of the file. This is only mutable on update when uploading new content. This field can be left blank, and the mimetype will be determined from the uploaded content's MIME type.
---@field downloadUrl? string Output only. Short lived download URL for the file. This field is only populated for files with content stored in Google Drive; it is not populated for Google Docs or shortcut files.
---@field hasThumbnail? boolean Output only. Whether this file has a thumbnail. This does not indicate whether the requesting app has access to the thumbnail. To check access, look for the presence of the thumbnailLink field.
---@field quotaBytesUsed? string Output only. The number of quota bytes used by this file.
---@field explicitlyTrashed? boolean Output only. Whether this file has been explicitly trashed, as opposed to recursively trashed.
---@field modifiedByMeDate? string Last time this file was modified by the user (formatted RFC 3339 timestamp). Note that setting modifiedDate will also update the modifiedByMe date for the user which set the date.
---@field thumbnailLink? string Output only. A short-lived link to the file's thumbnail, if available. Typically lasts on the order of hours. Not intended for direct usage on web applications due to [Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/CORS), consider using a proxy server. Only populated when the requesting app can access the file's content. If the file isn't shared publicly, the URL returned in `Files.thumbnailLink` must be fetched using a credentialed request.
---@field headRevisionId? string Output only. The ID of the file's head revision. This field is only populated for files with content stored in Google Drive; it is not populated for Docs Editors or shortcut files.
---@field parents? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.ParentReferenceList The ID of the parent folder containing the file. A file can only have one parent folder; specifying multiple parents isn't supported. If not specified as part of an insert request, the file is placed directly in the user's My Drive folder. If not specified as part of a copy request, the file inherits any discoverable parent of the source file. Update requests must use the `addParents` and `removeParents` parameters to modify the parents list.
---@field userPermission? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.Permission Output only. The permissions for the authenticated user on this file.
---@field embedLink? string Output only. A link for embedding the file.
---@field shareable? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `capabilities/canShare` instead.
---@field sha1Checksum? string Output only. The SHA1 checksum associated with this file, if available. This field is only populated for files with content stored in Google Drive; it is not populated for Docs Editors or shortcut files.
---@field etag? string Output only. ETag of the file.
---@field hasAugmentedPermissions? boolean Output only. Whether there are permissions directly on this file. This field is only populated for items in shared drives.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileCapabilities
---@field canDisableInheritedPermissions? boolean Output only. Whether a user can disable inherited permissions.
---@field canMoveItemIntoTeamDrive? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `canMoveItemOutOfDrive` instead.
---@field canModifyLabels? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can modify the labels on the file.
---@field canUntrash? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can restore this file from trash.
---@field canMoveChildrenOutOfTeamDrive? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `canMoveChildrenOutOfDrive` instead.
---@field canAddChildren? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can add children to this folder. This is always false when the item is not a folder.
---@field canMoveTeamDriveItem? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `canMoveItemWithinDrive` or `canMoveItemOutOfDrive` instead.
---@field canReadLabels? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can read the labels on the file.
---@field canComment? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can comment on this file.
---@field canReadTeamDrive? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `canReadDrive` instead.
---@field canReadRevisions? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can read the revisions resource of this file. For a shared drive item, whether revisions of non-folder descendants of this item, or this item itself if it is not a folder, can be read.
---@field canDelete? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can delete this file.
---@field canCopy? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can copy this file. For an item in a shared drive, whether the current user can copy non-folder descendants of this item, or this item itself if it is not a folder.
---@field canMoveChildrenWithinDrive? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can move children of this folder within this drive. This is false when the item is not a folder. Note that a request to move the child may still fail depending on the current user's access to the child and to the destination folder.
---@field canModifyContentRestriction? boolean Deprecated: Output only. Use one of `canModifyEditorContentRestriction`, `canModifyOwnerContentRestriction` or `canRemoveContentRestriction`.
---@field canMoveItemOutOfTeamDrive? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `canMoveItemOutOfDrive` instead.
---@field canRemoveChildren? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can remove children from this folder. This is always false when the item is not a folder. For a folder in a shared drive, use `canDeleteChildren` or `canTrashChildren` instead.
---@field canMoveChildrenWithinTeamDrive? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `canMoveChildrenWithinDrive` instead.
---@field canRename? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can rename this file.
---@field canMoveChildrenOutOfDrive? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can move children of this folder outside of the shared drive. This is false when the item is not a folder. Only populated for items in shared drives.
---@field canAddMyDriveParent? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can add a parent for the item without removing an existing parent in the same request. Not populated for shared drive files.
---@field canMoveItemOutOfDrive? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can move this item outside of this drive by changing its parent. Note that a request to change the parent of the item may still fail depending on the new parent that is being added.
---@field canMoveItemWithinTeamDrive? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `canMoveItemWithinDrive` instead.
---@field canListChildren? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can list the children of this folder. This is always false when the item is not a folder.
---@field canModifyEditorContentRestriction? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can add or modify content restrictions on the file which are editor restricted.
---@field canReadDrive? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can read the shared drive to which this file belongs. Only populated for items in shared drives.
---@field canChangeCopyRequiresWriterPermission? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can change the `copyRequiresWriterPermission` restriction of this file.
---@field canChangeSecurityUpdateEnabled? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can change the securityUpdateEnabled field on link share metadata.
---@field canEnableInheritedPermissions? boolean Output only. Whether a user can re-enable inherited permissions.
---@field canAcceptOwnership? boolean Output only. Whether the current user is the pending owner of the file. Not populated for shared drive files.
---@field canTrashChildren? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can trash children of this folder. This is false when the item is not a folder. Only populated for items in shared drives.
---@field canDeleteChildren? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can delete children of this folder. This is false when the item is not a folder. Only populated for items in shared drives.
---@field canChangeRestrictedDownload? boolean Output only. Deprecated.
---@field canAddFolderFromAnotherDrive? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can add a folder from another drive (different shared drive or My Drive) to this folder. This is false when the item is not a folder. Only populated for items in shared drives.
---@field canShare? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can modify the sharing settings for this file.
---@field canDownload? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can download this file.
---@field canRemoveMyDriveParent? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can remove a parent from the item without adding another parent in the same request. Not populated for shared drive files.
---@field canModifyOwnerContentRestriction? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can add or modify content restrictions which are owner restricted.
---@field canRemoveContentRestriction? boolean Output only. Whether there is a content restriction on the file that can be removed by the current user.
---@field canEdit? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can edit this file. Other factors may limit the type of changes a user can make to a file. For example, see `canChangeCopyRequiresWriterPermission` or `canModifyContent`.
---@field canMoveItemWithinDrive? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can move this item within this drive. Note that a request to change the parent of the item may still fail depending on the new parent that is being added and the parent that is being removed.
---@field canTrash? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can move this file to trash.
---@field canModifyContent? boolean Output only. Whether the current user can modify the content of this file.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileImageMediaMetadata
---@field colorSpace? string Output only. The color space of the photo.
---@field whiteBalance? string Output only. The white balance mode used to create the photo.
---@field aperture? number Output only. The aperture used to create the photo (f-number).
---@field isoSpeed? number Output only. The ISO speed used to create the photo.
---@field exposureMode? string Output only. The exposure mode used to create the photo.
---@field meteringMode? string Output only. The metering mode used to create the photo.
---@field sensor? string Output only. The type of sensor used to create the photo.
---@field exposureBias? number Output only. The exposure bias of the photo (APEX value).
---@field rotation? number Output only. The number of clockwise 90 degree rotations applied from the image's original orientation.
---@field flashUsed? boolean Output only. Whether a flash was used to create the photo.
---@field height? number Output only. The height of the image in pixels.
---@field focalLength? number Output only. The focal length used to create the photo, in millimeters.
---@field date? string Output only. The date and time the photo was taken (EXIF format timestamp).
---@field subjectDistance? number Output only. The distance to the subject of the photo, in meters.
---@field cameraMake? string Output only. The make of the camera used to create the photo.
---@field location? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileImageMediaMetadataLocation Output only. Geographic location information stored in the image.
---@field lens? string Output only. The lens used to create the photo.
---@field width? number Output only. The width of the image in pixels.
---@field cameraModel? string Output only. The model of the camera used to create the photo.
---@field maxApertureValue? number Output only. The smallest f-number of the lens at the focal length used to create the photo (APEX value).
---@field exposureTime? number Output only. The length of the exposure, in seconds.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileImageMediaMetadataLocation
---@field longitude? number Output only. The longitude stored in the image.
---@field latitude? number Output only. The latitude stored in the image.
---@field altitude? number Output only. The altitude stored in the image.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileIndexableText
---@field text? string The text to be indexed for this file.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileLabelInfo
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.LabelList_ Output only. The set of labels on the file as requested by the label IDs in the `includeLabels` parameter. By default, no labels are returned.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileLabels
---@field restricted? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `copyRequiresWriterPermission` instead.
---@field trashed? boolean Whether this file has been trashed. This label applies to all users accessing the file; however, only owners are allowed to see and untrash files.
---@field modified? boolean Output only. Whether the file has been modified by this user.
---@field starred? boolean Whether this file is starred by the user.
---@field viewed? boolean Whether this file has been viewed by this user.
---@field hidden? boolean Output only. Deprecated.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileLinkShareMetadata
---@field securityUpdateEligible? boolean Output only. Whether the file is eligible for security update.
---@field securityUpdateEnabled? boolean Output only. Whether the security update is enabled for this file.

---A list of files.
---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileList
---@field items gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileList_ The list of files. If nextPageToken is populated, then this list may be incomplete and an additional page of results should be fetched.
---@field nextPageToken? string The page token for the next page of files. This will be absent if the end of the files list has been reached. If the token is rejected for any reason, it should be discarded, and pagination should be restarted from the first page of results.
---@field kind? string This is always `drive#fileList`.
---@field etag? string The ETag of the list.
---@field selfLink? string A link back to this list.
---@field nextLink? string A link to the next page of files.
---@field incompleteSearch? boolean Whether the search process was incomplete. If true, then some search results may be missing, since all documents were not searched. This may occur when searching multiple drives with the "allDrives" corpora, but all corpora could not be searched. When this happens, it is suggested that clients narrow their query by choosing a different corpus such as "default" or "drive".

---@alias gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileList_ gcp.unstable.drive_v2.File[]

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileShortcutDetails
---@field targetMimeType? string Output only. The MIME type of the file that this shortcut points to. The value of this field is a snapshot of the target's MIME type, captured when the shortcut is created.
---@field targetResourceKey? string Output only. The ResourceKey for the target file.
---@field targetId? string The ID of the file that this shortcut points to. Can only be set on `files.insert` requests.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileThumbnail
---@field image? string The URL-safe Base64 encoded bytes of the thumbnail image. It should conform to RFC 4648 section 5.
---@field mimeType? string The MIME type of the thumbnail.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileVideoMediaMetadata
---@field durationMillis? string Output only. The duration of the video in milliseconds.
---@field width? number Output only. The width of the video in pixels.
---@field height? number Output only. The height of the video in pixels.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.GenerateCseTokenFilesRequest
---@field fileId? string The ID of the file for which the JWT should be generated. If not provided, an id will be generated.
---@field parent? string The ID of the expected parent of the file. Used when generating a JWT for a new CSE file. If specified, the parent will be fetched, and if the parent is a shared drive item, the shared drive's policy will be used to determine the KACLS that should be used. It is invalid to specify both file_id and parent in a single request.

---JWT and associated metadata used to generate CSE files.
---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.GenerateCseTokenResponse
---@field currentKaclsId? string The current Key ACL Service (KACLS) ID associated with the JWT.
---@field kind? string Output only. Identifies what kind of resource this is. Value: the fixed string `"drive#generateCseTokenResponse"`.
---@field currentKaclsName? string Name of the KACLs that the returned KACLs ID points to.
---@field jwt? string The signed JSON Web Token (JWT) for the file.
---@field fileId? string The fileId for which the JWT was generated.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.GenerateIdsFilesRequest
---@field space? string The space in which the IDs can be used to create new files. Supported values are `drive` and `appDataFolder`. (Default: `drive`)
---@field maxResults? number Maximum number of IDs to return.
---@field type? string The type of items which the IDs can be used for. Supported values are `files` and `shortcuts`. Note that `shortcuts` are only supported in the `drive` `space`. (Default: `files`)

---A list of generated IDs which can be provided in insert requests
---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.GeneratedIds
---@field ids? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringList The IDs generated for the requesting user in the specified space.
---@field space? string The type of file that can be created with these IDs.
---@field kind? string This is always `drive#generatedIds`

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.GetAboutRequest
---@field includeSubscribed? boolean Whether to count changes outside the My Drive hierarchy. When set to false, changes to files such as those in the Application Data folder or shared files which have not been added to My Drive will be omitted from the `maxChangeIdCount`.
---@field startChangeId? string Change ID to start counting from when calculating number of remaining change IDs
---@field maxChangeIdCount? string Maximum number of remaining change IDs to count

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.GetAppsRequest
---@field appId string The ID of the app.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.GetChangesRequest
---@field changeId string The ID of the change.
---@field teamDriveId? string Deprecated: Use `driveId` instead.
---@field supportsTeamDrives? boolean Deprecated: Use `supportsAllDrives` instead.
---@field driveId? string The shared drive from which the change will be returned.
---@field supportsAllDrives? boolean Whether the requesting application supports both My Drives and shared drives.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.GetChildrenRequest
---@field folderId string The ID of the folder.
---@field childId string The ID of the child.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.GetCommentsRequest
---@field commentId string The ID of the comment.
---@field fileId string The ID of the file.
---@field includeDeleted? boolean If set, this will succeed when retrieving a deleted comment, and will include any deleted replies.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.GetDrivesRequest
---@field driveId string The ID of the shared drive.
