---@field etag? string The ETag of the list.
---@field selfLink? string A link back to this list.
---@field items gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PermissionList_ The list of permissions.
---@field nextPageToken? string The page token for the next page of permissions. This field will be absent if the end of the permissions list has been reached. If the token is rejected for any reason, it should be discarded, and pagination should be restarted from the first page of results.
---@field kind? string This is always `drive#permissionList`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PermissionList_ gcp.unstable.drive_v2.Permission[]

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PermissionPermissionDetailsItem
---@field additionalRoles? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringList Output only. Additional roles for this user. Only `commenter` is currently possible, though more may be supported in the future.
---@field permissionType? string Output only. The permission type for this user. While new values may be added in future, the following are currently possible: * `file` * `member`
---@field inherited? boolean Output only. Whether this permission is inherited. This field is always populated.
---@field inheritedFrom? string Output only. The ID of the item from which this permission is inherited. This is only populated for items in shared drives.
---@field role? string Output only. The primary role for this user. While new values may be added in the future, the following are currently possible: * `organizer` * `fileOrganizer` * `writer` * `reader`

---@alias gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PermissionPermissionDetailsItemList gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PermissionPermissionDetailsItem[]

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PermissionTeamDrivePermissionDetailsItem
---@field role? string Output only. Deprecated: Use `permissionDetails/role` instead.
---@field inherited? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `permissionDetails/inherited` instead.
---@field inheritedFrom? string Output only. Deprecated: Use `permissionDetails/inheritedFrom` instead.
---@field additionalRoles? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringList Output only. Deprecated: Use `permissionDetails/additionalRoles` instead.
---@field teamDrivePermissionType? string Output only. Deprecated: Use `permissionDetails/permissionType` instead.

---@alias gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PermissionTeamDrivePermissionDetailsItemList gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PermissionTeamDrivePermissionDetailsItem[]

---A key-value pair attached to a file that is either public or private to an application. The following limits apply to file properties: * Maximum of 100 properties total per file * Maximum of 30 private properties per app * Maximum of 30 public properties * Maximum of 124 bytes size limit on (key + value) string in UTF-8 encoding for a single property Some resource methods (such as `properties.update`) require a `propertyKey`. Use the `properties.list` method to retrieve the key for a property.
---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.Property
---@field key? string The key of this property.
---@field kind? string Output only. This is always `drive#property`.
---@field value? string The value of this property.
---@field visibility? string The visibility of this property. Allowed values are PRIVATE (default) and PUBLIC. Private properties can only be retrieved using an authenticated request. An authenticated request uses an access token obtained with a OAuth 2 client ID. You cannot use an API key to retrieve private properties.
---@field etag? string Output only. ETag of the property.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. The link back to this property.

---A collection of properties, key-value pairs that are either public or private to an application.
---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PropertyList
---@field etag? string The ETag of the list.
---@field items? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PropertyList_ The list of properties.
---@field selfLink? string The link back to this list.
---@field kind? string This is always `drive#propertyList`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PropertyList_ gcp.unstable.drive_v2.Property[]

---A revision of a file. Some resource methods (such as `revisions.update`) require a `revisionId`. Use the `revisions.list` method to retrieve the ID for a revision.
---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.Revision
---@field kind? string Output only. This is always `drive#revision`.
---@field originalFilename? string Output only. The original filename when this revision was created. This will only be populated on files with content stored in Drive.
---@field lastModifyingUserName? string Output only. Name of the last user to modify this revision.
---@field fileSize? string Output only. The size of the revision in bytes. This will only be populated on files with content stored in Drive.
---@field etag? string Output only. The ETag of the revision.
---@field md5Checksum? string Output only. An MD5 checksum for the content of this revision. This will only be populated on files with content stored in Drive.
---@field downloadUrl? string Output only. Short term download URL for the file. This will only be populated on files with content stored in Drive.
---@field publishedLink? string Output only. A link to the published revision. This is only populated for Docs Editors files.
---@field lastModifyingUser? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.User Output only. The last user to modify this revision. This field is only populated when the last modification was performed by a signed-in user.
---@field publishAuto? boolean Whether subsequent revisions will be automatically republished. This is only populated and can only be modified for Docs Editors files.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. A link back to this revision.
---@field published? boolean Whether this revision is published. This is only populated and can only be modified for Docs Editors files.
---@field pinned? boolean Whether this revision is pinned to prevent automatic purging. If not set, the revision is automatically purged 30 days after newer content is uploaded. This field can only be modified on files with content stored in Drive, excluding Docs Editors files. Revisions can also be pinned when they are created through the drive.files.insert/update/copy by using the pinned query parameter. Pinned revisions are stored indefinitely using additional storage quota, up to a maximum of 200 revisions.
---@field modifiedDate? string Last time this revision was modified (formatted RFC 3339 timestamp).
---@field exportLinks? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringMap Output only. Links for exporting Docs Editors files to specific formats.
---@field id? string Output only. The ID of the revision.
---@field mimeType? string Output only. The MIME type of the revision.
---@field publishedOutsideDomain? boolean Whether this revision is published outside the domain. This is only populated and can only be modified for Docs Editors files.

---A list of revisions of a file.
---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.RevisionList
---@field selfLink? string A link back to this list.
---@field kind? string This is always `drive#revisionList`.
---@field items gcp.unstable.drive_v2.RevisionList_ The list of revisions. If nextPageToken is populated, then this list may be incomplete and an additional page of results should be fetched.
---@field nextPageToken? string The page token for the next page of revisions. This field will be absent if the end of the revisions list has been reached. If the token is rejected for any reason, it should be discarded and pagination should be restarted from the first page of results.
---@field etag? string The ETag of the list.

---@alias gcp.unstable.drive_v2.RevisionList_ gcp.unstable.drive_v2.Revision[]

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StartPageToken
---@field startPageToken? string The starting page token for listing changes.
---@field kind? string Identifies what kind of resource this is. Value: the fixed string `"drive#startPageToken"`.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StopChannelsRequest
---@field kind? string Identifies this as a notification channel used to watch for changes to a resource, which is `api#channel`.
---@field id? string A UUID or similar unique string that identifies this channel.
---@field resourceId? string An opaque ID that identifies the resource being watched on this channel. Stable across different API versions.
---@field token? string An arbitrary string delivered to the target address with each notification delivered over this channel. Optional.
---@field payload? boolean A Boolean value to indicate whether payload is wanted. Optional.
---@field resourceUri? string A version-specific identifier for the watched resource.
---@field address? string The address where notifications are delivered for this channel.
---@field type? string The type of delivery mechanism used for this channel. Valid values are "web_hook" or "webhook".
---@field expiration? string Date and time of notification channel expiration, expressed as a Unix timestamp, in milliseconds. Optional.
---@field params? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringMap Additional parameters controlling delivery channel behavior. Optional.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StopChannelsResponse

---@alias gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringList string[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringMap { [string]: string }

---Deprecated: Use the `drive` collection instead.
---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TeamDrive
---@field restrictions? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TeamDriveRestrictions A set of restrictions that apply to this Team Drive or items inside this Team Drive.
---@field createdDate? string The time at which the Team Drive was created (RFC 3339 date-time).
---@field backgroundImageFile? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TeamDriveBackgroundImageFile An image file and cropping parameters from which a background image for this Team Drive is set. This is a write only field; it can only be set on `drive.teamdrives.update` requests that don't set `themeId`. When specified, all fields of the `backgroundImageFile` must be set.
---@field backgroundImageLink? string A short-lived link to this Team Drive's background image.
---@field name? string The name of this Team Drive.
---@field kind? string This is always `drive#teamDrive`
---@field colorRgb? string The color of this Team Drive as an RGB hex string. It can only be set on a `drive.teamdrives.update` request that does not set `themeId`.
---@field capabilities? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TeamDriveCapabilities Capabilities the current user has on this Team Drive.
---@field themeId? string The ID of the theme from which the background image and color will be set. The set of possible `teamDriveThemes` can be retrieved from a `drive.about.get` response. When not specified on a `drive.teamdrives.insert` request, a random theme is chosen from which the background image and color are set. This is a write-only field; it can only be set on requests that don't set `colorRgb` or `backgroundImageFile`.
---@field id? string The ID of this Team Drive which is also the ID of the top level folder of this Team Drive.
---@field orgUnitId? string The organizational unit of this shared drive. This field is only populated on `drives.list` responses when the `useDomainAdminAccess` parameter is set to `true`.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TeamDriveBackgroundImageFile
---@field xCoordinate? number The X coordinate of the upper left corner of the cropping area in the background image. This is a value in the closed range of 0 to 1. This value represents the horizontal distance from the left side of the entire image to the left side of the cropping area divided by the width of the entire image.
---@field yCoordinate? number The Y coordinate of the upper left corner of the cropping area in the background image. This is a value in the closed range of 0 to 1. This value represents the vertical distance from the top side of the entire image to the top side of the cropping area divided by the height of the entire image.
---@field id? string The ID of an image file in Drive to use for the background image.
---@field width? number The width of the cropped image in the closed range of 0 to 1. This value represents the width of the cropped image divided by the width of the entire image. The height is computed by applying a width to height aspect ratio of 80 to 9. The resulting image must be at least 1280 pixels wide and 144 pixels high.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TeamDriveCapabilities
---@field canEdit? boolean Whether the current user can edit files in this Team Drive
---@field canDeleteChildren? boolean Whether the current user can delete children from folders in this Team Drive.
---@field canDeleteTeamDrive? boolean Whether the current user can delete this Team Drive. Attempting to delete the Team Drive may still fail if there are untrashed items inside the Team Drive.
---@field canRemoveChildren? boolean Deprecated: Use `canDeleteChildren` or `canTrashChildren` instead.
---@field canManageMembers? boolean Whether the current user can add members to this Team Drive or remove them or change their role.
---@field canChangeTeamMembersOnlyRestriction? boolean Whether the current user can change the `teamMembersOnly` restriction of this Team Drive.
---@field canCopy? boolean Whether the current user can copy files in this Team Drive.
---@field canRename? boolean Whether the current user can rename files or folders in this Team Drive.
---@field canChangeSharingFoldersRequiresOrganizerPermissionRestriction? boolean Whether the current user can change the `sharingFoldersRequiresOrganizerPermission` restriction of this Team Drive.
---@field canShare? boolean Whether the current user can share files or folders in this Team Drive.
---@field canResetTeamDriveRestrictions? boolean Whether the current user can reset the Team Drive restrictions to defaults.
---@field canChangeDomainUsersOnlyRestriction? boolean Whether the current user can change the `domainUsersOnly` restriction of this Team Drive.
---@field canChangeCopyRequiresWriterPermissionRestriction? boolean Whether the current user can change the `copyRequiresWriterPermission` restriction of this Team Drive.
---@field canChangeTeamDriveBackground? boolean Whether the current user can change the background of this Team Drive.
---@field canListChildren? boolean Whether the current user can list the children of folders in this Team Drive.
---@field canReadRevisions? boolean Whether the current user can read the revisions resource of files in this Team Drive.
---@field canTrashChildren? boolean Whether the current user can trash children from folders in this Team Drive.
---@field canComment? boolean Whether the current user can comment on files in this Team Drive.
---@field canAddChildren? boolean Whether the current user can add children to folders in this Team Drive.
---@field canRenameTeamDrive? boolean Whether the current user can rename this Team Drive.
---@field canDownload? boolean Whether the current user can download files in this Team Drive.

---A list of Team Drives.
---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TeamDriveList
---@field kind? string This is always `drive#teamDriveList`
---@field items gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TeamDriveList_ The list of Team Drives.
---@field nextPageToken? string The page token for the next page of Team Drives.

---@alias gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TeamDriveList_ gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TeamDrive[]

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TeamDriveRestrictions
---@field teamMembersOnly? boolean Whether access to items inside this Team Drive is restricted to members of this Team Drive.
---@field adminManagedRestrictions? boolean Whether administrative privileges on this Team Drive are required to modify restrictions.
---@field copyRequiresWriterPermission? boolean Whether the options to copy, print, or download files inside this Team Drive, should be disabled for readers and commenters. When this restriction is set to `true`, it will override the similarly named field to `true` for any file inside this Team Drive.
---@field sharingFoldersRequiresOrganizerPermission? boolean If true, only users with the organizer role can share folders. If false, users with either the organizer role or the file organizer role can share folders.
---@field domainUsersOnly? boolean Whether access to this Team Drive and items inside this Team Drive is restricted to users of the domain to which this Team Drive belongs. This restriction may be overridden by other sharing policies controlled outside of this Team Drive.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TouchFilesRequest
---@field fileId string The ID of the file to update.
---@field supportsAllDrives? boolean Whether the requesting application supports both My Drives and shared drives.
---@field supportsTeamDrives? boolean Deprecated: Use `supportsAllDrives` instead.
---@field includePermissionsForView? string Specifies which additional view's permissions to include in the response. Only `published` is supported.
---@field includeLabels? string A comma-separated list of IDs of labels to include in the `labelInfo` part of the response.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TrashFilesRequest
---@field supportsAllDrives? boolean Whether the requesting application supports both My Drives and shared drives.
---@field includeLabels? string A comma-separated list of IDs of labels to include in the `labelInfo` part of the response.
---@field supportsTeamDrives? boolean Deprecated: Use `supportsAllDrives` instead.
---@field includePermissionsForView? string Specifies which additional view's permissions to include in the response. Only `published` is supported.
---@field fileId string The ID of the file to trash.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UnhideDrivesRequest
---@field driveId string The ID of the shared drive.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UntrashFilesRequest
---@field fileId string The ID of the file to untrash.
---@field includePermissionsForView? string Specifies which additional view's permissions to include in the response. Only `published` is supported.
---@field supportsTeamDrives? boolean Deprecated: Use `supportsAllDrives` instead.
---@field supportsAllDrives? boolean Whether the requesting application supports both My Drives and shared drives.
---@field includeLabels? string A comma-separated list of IDs of labels to include in the `labelInfo` part of the response.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UpdateCommentsRequest
---@field content? string The plain text content used to create this comment. This is not HTML safe and should only be used as a starting point to make edits to a comment's content.
---@field selfLink? string A link back to this comment.
---@field context? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.CommentContext Context of a file which is being commented on.
---@field replies? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.CommentReplyList_ Replies to this post.
---@field htmlContent? string HTML formatted content for this comment.
---@field deleted? boolean Whether this comment has been deleted. If a comment has been deleted the content will be cleared and this will only represent a comment that once existed.
---@field anchor? string A region of the document represented as a JSON string. For details on defining anchor properties, refer to [Manage comments and replies](https://developers.google.com/workspace/drive/api/v3/manage-comments).
---@field author? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.User The user who wrote this comment.
---@field createdDate? string The date when this comment was first created.
---@field fileTitle? string The title of the file which this comment is addressing.
---@field modifiedDate? string The date when this comment or any of its replies were last modified.
---@field status? string The status of this comment. Status can be changed by posting a reply to a comment with the desired status. Possible values are: * `open` - The comment is still open. * `resolved` - The comment has been resolved by one of its replies.
---@field kind? string This is always drive#comment.
---@field fileId string The ID of the file.
---@field commentId string The ID of the comment.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UpdateDrivesRequest
---@field backgroundImageLink? string Output only. A short-lived link to this shared drive's background image.
---@field restrictions? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.DriveRestrictions A set of restrictions that apply to this shared drive or items inside this shared drive.
---@field hidden? boolean Whether the shared drive is hidden from default view.
---@field backgroundImageFile? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.DriveBackgroundImageFile An image file and cropping parameters from which a background image for this shared drive is set. This is a write only field; it can only be set on `drive.drives.update` requests that don't set `themeId`. When specified, all fields of the `backgroundImageFile` must be set.
---@field colorRgb? string The color of this shared drive as an RGB hex string. It can only be set on a `drive.drives.update` request that does not set `themeId`.
---@field createdDate? string The time at which the shared drive was created (RFC 3339 date-time).
---@field themeId? string The ID of the theme from which the background image and color will be set. The set of possible `driveThemes` can be retrieved from a `drive.about.get` response. When not specified on a `drive.drives.insert` request, a random theme is chosen from which the background image and color are set. This is a write-only field; it can only be set on requests that don't set `colorRgb` or `backgroundImageFile`.
---@field name? string The name of this shared drive.
---@field kind? string Output only. This is always `drive#drive`
---@field capabilities? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.DriveCapabilities Output only. Capabilities the current user has on this shared drive.
---@field id? string Output only. The ID of this shared drive which is also the ID of the top level folder of this shared drive.
---@field orgUnitId? string Output only. The organizational unit of this shared drive. This field is only populated on `drives.list` responses when the `useDomainAdminAccess` parameter is set to `true`.
---@field useDomainAdminAccess? boolean Issue the request as a domain administrator; if set to true, then the requester will be granted access if they are an administrator of the domain to which the shared drive belongs.
---@field driveId string The ID of the shared drive.

---@alias gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UpdateFilesModifiedDateBehaviorEnum "fromBody"|"fromBodyIfNeeded"|"fromBodyOrNow"|"noChange"|"now"|"nowIfNeeded"

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UpdateFilesRequest
---@field canReadRevisions? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `capabilities/canReadRevisions` instead.
---@field sharingUser? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.User Output only. User that shared the item with the current user, if available.
---@field labelInfo? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileLabelInfo Output only. An overview of the labels on the file.
---@field alternateLink? string Output only. A link for opening the file in a relevant Google editor or viewer.
---@field sha256Checksum? string Output only. The SHA256 checksum associated with this file, if available. This field is only populated for files with content stored in Google Drive; it is not populated for Docs Editors or shortcut files.
---@field shared? boolean Output only. Whether the file has been shared. Not populated for items in shared drives.
---@field capabilities? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileCapabilities Output only. Capabilities the current user has on this file. Each capability corresponds to a fine-grained action that a user may take.
---@field editable? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `capabilities/canEdit` instead.
---@field owners? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UserList Output only. The owner of this file. Only certain legacy files may have more than one owner. This field isn't populated for items in shared drives.
---@field videoMediaMetadata? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileVideoMediaMetadata Output only. Metadata about video media. This will only be present for video types.
---@field ownerNames? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringList Output only. Name(s) of the owner(s) of this file. Not populated for items in shared drives.
---@field originalFilename? string The original filename of the uploaded content if available, or else the original value of the `title` field. This is only available for files with binary content in Google Drive.
---@field title? string The title of this file. Note that for immutable items such as the top level folders of shared drives, My Drive root folder, and Application Data folder the title is constant.
---@field exportLinks? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringMap Output only. Links for exporting Docs Editors files to specific formats.
---@field kind? string Output only. The type of file. This is always `drive#file`.
---@field description? string A short description of the file.
---@field sharedWithMeDate? string Time at which this file was shared with the user (formatted RFC 3339 timestamp).
---@field indexableText? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileIndexableText Indexable text attributes for the file (can only be written)
---@field createdDate? string Create time for this file (formatted RFC 3339 timestamp).
---@field copyRequiresWriterPermission? boolean Whether the options to copy, print, or download this file, should be disabled for readers and commenters.
---@field defaultOpenWithLink? string Output only. A link to open this file with the user's default app for this file. Only populated when the drive.apps.readonly scope is used.
---@field inheritedPermissionsDisabled? boolean Whether this file has inherited permissions disabled. Inherited permissions are enabled by default.
---@field md5Checksum? string Output only. An MD5 checksum for the content of this file. This field is only populated for files with content stored in Google Drive; it is not populated for Docs Editors or shortcut files.
---@field openWithLinks? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringMap Output only. A map of the id of each of the user's apps to a link to open this file with that app. Only populated when the drive.apps.readonly scope is used.
---@field canComment? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `capabilities/canComment` instead.
---@field modifiedDate? string Last time this file was modified by anyone (formatted RFC 3339 timestamp). This is only mutable on update when the setModifiedDate parameter is set.
---@field writersCanShare? boolean Whether writers can share the document with other users. Not populated for items in shared drives.
---@field fileSize? string Output only. Size in bytes of blobs and first party editor files. Won't be populated for files that have no size, like shortcuts and folders.
---@field thumbnailVersion? string Output only. The thumbnail version for use in thumbnail cache invalidation.
---@field lastModifyingUser? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.User Output only. The last user to modify this file. This field is only populated when the last modification was performed by a signed-in user.
---@field webViewLink? string Output only. A link only available on public folders for viewing their static web assets (HTML, CSS, JS, etc) via Google Drive's Website Hosting.
---@field fileExtension? string Output only. The final component of `fullFileExtension` with trailing text that does not appear to be part of the extension removed. This field is only populated for files with content stored in Google Drive; it is not populated for Docs Editors or shortcut files.
---@field trashedDate? string The time that the item was trashed (formatted RFC 3339 timestamp). Only populated for items in shared drives.
---@field driveId? string Output only. ID of the shared drive the file resides in. Only populated for items in shared drives.
---@field shortcutDetails? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileShortcutDetails Shortcut file details. Only populated for shortcut files, which have the mimeType field set to `application/vnd.google-apps.shortcut`. Can only be set on `files.insert` requests.
---@field permissionIds? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringList Output only. List of permission IDs for users with access to this file.
---@field ownedByMe? boolean Output only. Whether the file is owned by the current user. Not populated for items in shared drives.
---@field teamDriveId? string Output only. Deprecated: Use `driveId` instead.
---@field folderColorRgb? string Folder color as an RGB hex string if the file is a folder or a shortcut to a folder. The list of supported colors is available in the folderColorPalette field of the About resource. If an unsupported color is specified, it will be changed to the closest color in the palette.
---@field resourceKey? string Output only. A key needed to access the item via a shared link.
---@field fullFileExtension? string Output only. The full file extension; extracted from the title. May contain multiple concatenated extensions, such as "tar.gz". Removing an extension from the title does not clear this field; however, changing the extension on the title does update this field. This field is only populated for files with content stored in Google Drive; it is not populated for Docs Editors or shortcut files.
---@field clientEncryptionDetails? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.ClientEncryptionDetails Client Side Encryption related details. Contains details about the encryption state of the file and details regarding the encryption mechanism that clients need to use when decrypting the contents of this item. This will only be present on files and not on folders or shortcuts.
---@field version? string Output only. A monotonically increasing version number for the file. This reflects every change made to the file on the server, even those not visible to the requesting user.
---@field contentRestrictions? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.ContentRestrictionList Restrictions for accessing the content of the file. Only populated if such a restriction exists.
---@field imageMediaMetadata? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileImageMediaMetadata Output only. Metadata about image media. This will only be present for image types, and its contents will depend on what can be parsed from the image content.
---@field webContentLink? string Output only. A link for downloading the content of the file in a browser using cookie based authentication. In cases where the content is shared publicly, the content can be downloaded without any credentials.
---@field isAppAuthorized? boolean Output only. Whether the file was created or opened by the requesting app.
---@field trashingUser? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.User Output only. If the file has been explicitly trashed, the user who trashed it. Only populated for items in shared drives.
---@field properties? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PropertyList_ The list of properties.
---@field spaces? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringList Output only. The list of spaces which contain the file. Supported values are `drive`, `appDataFolder` and `photos`.
---@field linkShareMetadata? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileLinkShareMetadata Contains details about the link URLs that clients are using to refer to this item.
---@field iconLink? string Output only. A link to the file's icon.
---@field thumbnail? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileThumbnail A thumbnail for the file. This will only be used if a standard thumbnail cannot be generated.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. A link back to this file.
---@field copyable? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `capabilities/canCopy` instead.
---@field id? string The ID of the file.
---@field appDataContents? boolean Output only. Whether this file is in the Application Data folder.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.FileLabels A group of labels for the file.
---@field permissions? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PermissionList_ Output only. The list of permissions for users with access to this file. Not populated for items in shared drives.
---@field lastModifyingUserName? string Output only. Name of the last user to modify this file.
---@field lastViewedByMeDate? string Last time this file was viewed by the user (formatted RFC 3339 timestamp).
---@field markedViewedByMeDate? string Deprecated.
---@field mimeType? string The MIME type of the file. This is only mutable on update when uploading new content. This field can be left blank, and the mimetype will be determined from the uploaded content's MIME type.
---@field downloadUrl? string Output only. Short lived download URL for the file. This field is only populated for files with content stored in Google Drive; it is not populated for Google Docs or shortcut files.
---@field hasThumbnail? boolean Output only. Whether this file has a thumbnail. This does not indicate whether the requesting app has access to the thumbnail. To check access, look for the presence of the thumbnailLink field.
---@field quotaBytesUsed? string Output only. The number of quota bytes used by this file.
---@field explicitlyTrashed? boolean Output only. Whether this file has been explicitly trashed, as opposed to recursively trashed.
---@field modifiedByMeDate? string Last time this file was modified by the user (formatted RFC 3339 timestamp). Note that setting modifiedDate will also update the modifiedByMe date for the user which set the date.
---@field thumbnailLink? string Output only. A short-lived link to the file's thumbnail, if available. Typically lasts on the order of hours. Not intended for direct usage on web applications due to [Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/CORS), consider using a proxy server. Only populated when the requesting app can access the file's content. If the file isn't shared publicly, the URL returned in `Files.thumbnailLink` must be fetched using a credentialed request.
---@field headRevisionId? string Output only. The ID of the file's head revision. This field is only populated for files with content stored in Google Drive; it is not populated for Docs Editors or shortcut files.
---@field parents? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.ParentReferenceList The ID of the parent folder containing the file. A file can only have one parent folder; specifying multiple parents isn't supported. If not specified as part of an insert request, the file is placed directly in the user's My Drive folder. If not specified as part of a copy request, the file inherits any discoverable parent of the source file. Update requests must use the `addParents` and `removeParents` parameters to modify the parents list.
---@field userPermission? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.Permission Output only. The permissions for the authenticated user on this file.
---@field embedLink? string Output only. A link for embedding the file.
---@field shareable? boolean Output only. Deprecated: Use `capabilities/canShare` instead.
---@field sha1Checksum? string Output only. The SHA1 checksum associated with this file, if available. This field is only populated for files with content stored in Google Drive; it is not populated for Docs Editors or shortcut files.
---@field etag? string Output only. ETag of the file.
---@field hasAugmentedPermissions? boolean Output only. Whether there are permissions directly on this file. This field is only populated for items in shared drives.
---@field updateViewedDate? boolean Whether to update the view date after successfully updating the file.
---@field setModifiedDate? boolean Whether to set the modified date using the value supplied in the request body. Setting this field to `true` is equivalent to `modifiedDateBehavior=fromBodyOrNow`, and `false` is equivalent to `modifiedDateBehavior=now`. To prevent any changes to the modified date set `modifiedDateBehavior=noChange`.
---@field timedTextTrackName? string The timed text track name.
---@field pinned? boolean Whether to pin the new revision. A file can have a maximum of 200 pinned revisions.
---@field addParents? string Comma-separated list of parent IDs to add.
---@field newRevision? boolean Whether a blob upload should create a new revision. If false, the blob data in the current head revision is replaced. If true or not set, a new blob is created as head revision, and previous unpinned revisions are preserved for a short period of time. Pinned revisions are stored indefinitely, using additional storage quota, up to a maximum of 200 revisions. For details on how revisions are retained, see the [Drive Help Center](https://support.google.com/drive/answer/2409045).
---@field ocr? boolean Whether to attempt OCR on .jpg, .png, .gif, or .pdf uploads.
---@field ocrLanguage? string If ocr is true, hints at the language to use. Valid values are BCP 47 codes.
---@field supportsAllDrives? boolean Whether the requesting application supports both My Drives and shared drives.
---@field includeLabels? string A comma-separated list of IDs of labels to include in the `labelInfo` part of the response.
---@field fileId string The ID of the file to update.
---@field enforceSingleParent? boolean Deprecated: Adding files to multiple folders is no longer supported. Use `shortcuts` instead.
---@field modifiedDateBehavior? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UpdateFilesModifiedDateBehaviorEnum|string Determines the behavior in which `modifiedDate` is updated. This overrides `setModifiedDate`.
---@field timedTextLanguage? string The language of the timed text.
---@field supportsTeamDrives? boolean Deprecated: Use `supportsAllDrives` instead.
---@field useContentAsIndexableText? boolean Whether to use the content as indexable text.
---@field includePermissionsForView? string Specifies which additional view's permissions to include in the response. Only `published` is supported.
---@field convert? boolean Deprecated: This parameter has no function.
---@field removeParents? string Comma-separated list of parent IDs to remove.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UpdatePermissionsRequest
---@field value? string The email address or domain name for the entity. This is used during inserts and is not populated in responses. When making a `drive.permissions.insert` request, exactly one of the `id` or `value` fields must be specified unless the permission type is `anyone`, in which case both `id` and `value` are ignored.
---@field domain? string Output only. The domain name of the entity this permission refers to. This is an output-only field which is present when the permission type is `user`, `group` or `domain`.
---@field pendingOwner? boolean Whether the account associated with this permission is a pending owner. Only populated for `user` type permissions for files that are not in a shared drive.
---@field additionalRoles? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringList Additional roles for this user. Only `commenter` is currently allowed, though more may be supported in the future.
---@field withLink? boolean Whether the link is required for this permission.
---@field permissionDetails? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PermissionPermissionDetailsItemList Output only. Details of whether the permissions on this item are inherited or directly on this item.
---@field role? string The primary role for this user. While new values may be supported in the future, the following are currently allowed: * `owner` * `organizer` * `fileOrganizer` * `writer` * `reader`
---@field teamDrivePermissionDetails? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.PermissionTeamDrivePermissionDetailsItemList Output only. Deprecated: Use `permissionDetails` instead.
---@field etag? string Output only. The ETag of the permission.
---@field deleted? boolean Output only. Whether the account associated with this permission has been deleted. This field only pertains to user and group permissions.
---@field name? string Output only. The name for this permission.
---@field kind? string Output only. This is always `drive#permission`.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. A link back to this permission.
---@field type? string The account type. Allowed values are: * `user` * `group` * `domain` * `anyone`
---@field expirationDate? string The time at which this permission will expire (RFC 3339 date-time). Expiration dates have the following restrictions: - They can only be set on user and group permissions - The date must be in the future - The date cannot be more than a year in the future - The date can only be set on drive.permissions.update or drive.permissions.patch requests
---@field id? string The ID of the user this permission refers to, and identical to the `permissionId` in the About and Files resources. When making a `drive.permissions.insert` request, exactly one of the `id` or `value` fields must be specified unless the permission type is `anyone`, in which case both `id` and `value` are ignored.
---@field emailAddress? string Output only. The email address of the user or group this permission refers to. This is an output-only field which is present when the permission type is `user` or `group`.
---@field authKey? string Output only. Deprecated.
---@field inheritedPermissionsDisabled? boolean When true, only organizers, owners, and users with permissions added directly on the item can access it.
---@field view? string Indicates the view for this permission. Only populated for permissions that belong to a view. published and metadata are the only supported values. - published: The permission's role is published_reader. - metadata: The item is only visible to the metadata view because the item has limited access and the scope has at least read access to the parent. Note: The metadata view is currently only supported on folders.
---@field photoLink? string Output only. A link to the profile photo, if available.
---@field enforceExpansiveAccess? boolean Deprecated: All requests use the expansive access rules.
---@field removeExpiration? boolean Whether to remove the expiration date.
---@field supportsTeamDrives? boolean Deprecated: Use `supportsAllDrives` instead.
---@field supportsAllDrives? boolean Whether the requesting application supports both My Drives and shared drives.
---@field fileId string The ID for the file or shared drive.
---@field useDomainAdminAccess? boolean Issue the request as a domain administrator; if set to true, then the requester will be granted access if the file ID parameter refers to a shared drive and the requester is an administrator of the domain to which the shared drive belongs.
---@field permissionId string The ID for the permission.
---@field transferOwnership? boolean Whether changing a role to `owner` downgrades the current owners to writers. Does nothing if the specified role is not `owner`.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UpdatePropertiesRequest
---@field key? string The key of this property.
---@field kind? string Output only. This is always `drive#property`.
---@field value? string The value of this property.
---@field etag? string Output only. ETag of the property.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. The link back to this property.
---@field propertyKey string The key of the property.
---@field fileId string The ID of the file.
---@field visibility? string The visibility of the property. Allowed values are PRIVATE and PUBLIC. (Default: PRIVATE)

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UpdateRepliesRequest
---@field modifiedDate? string The date when this reply was last modified.
---@field content? string The plain text content used to create this reply. This is not HTML safe and should only be used as a starting point to make edits to a reply's content. This field is required on inserts if no verb is specified (resolve/reopen).
---@field deleted? boolean Whether this reply has been deleted. If a reply has been deleted the content will be cleared and this will only represent a reply that once existed.
---@field kind? string This is always drive#commentReply.
---@field verb? string The action this reply performed to the parent comment. When creating a new reply this is the action to be perform tSo the parent comment. Possible values are: * `resolve` - To resolve a comment. * `reopen` - To reopen (un-resolve) a comment.
---@field htmlContent? string HTML formatted content for this reply.
---@field author? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.User The user who wrote this reply.
---@field createdDate? string The date when this reply was first created.
---@field fileId string The ID of the file.
---@field replyId string The ID of the reply.
---@field commentId string The ID of the comment.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UpdateRevisionsRequest
---@field kind? string Output only. This is always `drive#revision`.
---@field originalFilename? string Output only. The original filename when this revision was created. This will only be populated on files with content stored in Drive.
---@field lastModifyingUserName? string Output only. Name of the last user to modify this revision.
---@field fileSize? string Output only. The size of the revision in bytes. This will only be populated on files with content stored in Drive.
---@field etag? string Output only. The ETag of the revision.
---@field md5Checksum? string Output only. An MD5 checksum for the content of this revision. This will only be populated on files with content stored in Drive.
---@field downloadUrl? string Output only. Short term download URL for the file. This will only be populated on files with content stored in Drive.
---@field publishedLink? string Output only. A link to the published revision. This is only populated for Docs Editors files.
---@field lastModifyingUser? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.User Output only. The last user to modify this revision. This field is only populated when the last modification was performed by a signed-in user.
---@field publishAuto? boolean Whether subsequent revisions will be automatically republished. This is only populated and can only be modified for Docs Editors files.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. A link back to this revision.
---@field published? boolean Whether this revision is published. This is only populated and can only be modified for Docs Editors files.
---@field pinned? boolean Whether this revision is pinned to prevent automatic purging. If not set, the revision is automatically purged 30 days after newer content is uploaded. This field can only be modified on files with content stored in Drive, excluding Docs Editors files. Revisions can also be pinned when they are created through the drive.files.insert/update/copy by using the pinned query parameter. Pinned revisions are stored indefinitely using additional storage quota, up to a maximum of 200 revisions.
---@field modifiedDate? string Last time this revision was modified (formatted RFC 3339 timestamp).
---@field exportLinks? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringMap Output only. Links for exporting Docs Editors files to specific formats.
---@field id? string Output only. The ID of the revision.
---@field mimeType? string Output only. The MIME type of the revision.
---@field publishedOutsideDomain? boolean Whether this revision is published outside the domain. This is only populated and can only be modified for Docs Editors files.
---@field revisionId string The ID for the revision.
---@field fileId string The ID for the file.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UpdateTeamdrivesRequest
---@field restrictions? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TeamDriveRestrictions A set of restrictions that apply to this Team Drive or items inside this Team Drive.
---@field createdDate? string The time at which the Team Drive was created (RFC 3339 date-time).
---@field backgroundImageFile? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TeamDriveBackgroundImageFile An image file and cropping parameters from which a background image for this Team Drive is set. This is a write only field; it can only be set on `drive.teamdrives.update` requests that don't set `themeId`. When specified, all fields of the `backgroundImageFile` must be set.
---@field backgroundImageLink? string A short-lived link to this Team Drive's background image.
---@field name? string The name of this Team Drive.
---@field kind? string This is always `drive#teamDrive`
---@field colorRgb? string The color of this Team Drive as an RGB hex string. It can only be set on a `drive.teamdrives.update` request that does not set `themeId`.
---@field capabilities? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.TeamDriveCapabilities Capabilities the current user has on this Team Drive.
---@field themeId? string The ID of the theme from which the background image and color will be set. The set of possible `teamDriveThemes` can be retrieved from a `drive.about.get` response. When not specified on a `drive.teamdrives.insert` request, a random theme is chosen from which the background image and color are set. This is a write-only field; it can only be set on requests that don't set `colorRgb` or `backgroundImageFile`.
---@field id? string The ID of this Team Drive which is also the ID of the top level folder of this Team Drive.
---@field orgUnitId? string The organizational unit of this shared drive. This field is only populated on `drives.list` responses when the `useDomainAdminAccess` parameter is set to `true`.
---@field teamDriveId string The ID of the Team Drive
---@field useDomainAdminAccess? boolean Issue the request as a domain administrator; if set to true, then the requester will be granted access if they are an administrator of the domain to which the Team Drive belongs.

---Information about a Drive user.
---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.User
---@field emailAddress? string Output only. The email address of the user. This may not be present in certain contexts if the user has not made their email address visible to the requester.
---@field picture? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UserPicture Output only. The user's profile picture.
---@field permissionId? string Output only. The user's ID as visible in Permission resources.
---@field isAuthenticatedUser? boolean Output only. Whether this user is the same as the authenticated user for whom the request was made.
---@field kind? string Output only. Identifies what kind of resource this is. Value: the fixed string `drive#user`.
---@field displayName? string Output only. A plain text displayable name for this user.

---@alias gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UserList gcp.unstable.drive_v2.User[]

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.UserPicture
---@field url? string Output only. A URL that points to a profile picture of this user.

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.WatchChangesRequest
---@field kind? string Identifies this as a notification channel used to watch for changes to a resource, which is `api#channel`.
---@field id? string A UUID or similar unique string that identifies this channel.
---@field resourceId? string An opaque ID that identifies the resource being watched on this channel. Stable across different API versions.
---@field token? string An arbitrary string delivered to the target address with each notification delivered over this channel. Optional.
---@field payload? boolean A Boolean value to indicate whether payload is wanted. Optional.
---@field resourceUri? string A version-specific identifier for the watched resource.
---@field address? string The address where notifications are delivered for this channel.
---@field type? string The type of delivery mechanism used for this channel. Valid values are "web_hook" or "webhook".
---@field expiration? string Date and time of notification channel expiration, expressed as a Unix timestamp, in milliseconds. Optional.
---@field params? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringMap Additional parameters controlling delivery channel behavior. Optional.
---@field maxResults? number Maximum number of changes to return.
---@field pageToken? string The token for continuing a previous list request on the next page. This should be set to the value of `nextPageToken` from the previous response or to the response from the getStartPageToken method.
---@field includePermissionsForView? string Specifies which additional view's permissions to include in the response. Only `published` is supported.
---@field includeLabels? string A comma-separated list of IDs of labels to include in the `labelInfo` part of the response.
---@field startChangeId? string Deprecated: Use `pageToken` instead.
---@field includeTeamDriveItems? boolean Deprecated: Use `includeItemsFromAllDrives` instead.
---@field supportsTeamDrives? boolean Deprecated: Use `supportsAllDrives` instead.
---@field includeSubscribed? boolean Whether to include changes outside the My Drive hierarchy in the result. When set to false, changes to files such as those in the Application Data folder or shared files which have not been added to My Drive will be omitted from the result.
---@field supportsAllDrives? boolean Whether the requesting application supports both My Drives and shared drives.
---@field includeItemsFromAllDrives? boolean Whether both My Drive and shared drive items should be included in results.
---@field spaces? string A comma-separated list of spaces to query. Supported values are `drive`, `appDataFolder` and `photos`.
---@field includeDeleted? boolean Whether to include changes indicating that items have been removed from the list of changes, for example by deletion or loss of access.
---@field includeCorpusRemovals? boolean Whether changes should include the file resource if the file is still accessible by the user at the time of the request, even when a file was removed from the list of changes and there will be no further change entries for this file.
---@field driveId? string The shared drive from which changes will be returned. If specified the change IDs will be reflective of the shared drive; use the combined drive ID and change ID as an identifier.
---@field teamDriveId? string Deprecated: Use `driveId` instead.

---@alias gcp.unstable.drive_v2.WatchFilesProjectionEnum "BASIC"|"FULL"

---@class gcp.unstable.drive_v2.WatchFilesRequest
---@field kind? string Identifies this as a notification channel used to watch for changes to a resource, which is `api#channel`.
---@field id? string A UUID or similar unique string that identifies this channel.
---@field resourceId? string An opaque ID that identifies the resource being watched on this channel. Stable across different API versions.
---@field token? string An arbitrary string delivered to the target address with each notification delivered over this channel. Optional.
---@field payload? boolean A Boolean value to indicate whether payload is wanted. Optional.
---@field resourceUri? string A version-specific identifier for the watched resource.
---@field address? string The address where notifications are delivered for this channel.
---@field type? string The type of delivery mechanism used for this channel. Valid values are "web_hook" or "webhook".
---@field expiration? string Date and time of notification channel expiration, expressed as a Unix timestamp, in milliseconds. Optional.
---@field params? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.StringMap Additional parameters controlling delivery channel behavior. Optional.
---@field includePermissionsForView? string Specifies which additional view's permissions to include in the response. Only `published` is supported.
---@field supportsAllDrives? boolean Whether the requesting application supports both My Drives and shared drives.
---@field supportsTeamDrives? boolean Deprecated: Use `supportsAllDrives` instead.
---@field updateViewedDate? boolean Deprecated: Use files.update with modifiedDateBehavior=noChange, updateViewedDate=true and an empty request body.
---@field revisionId? string Specifies the Revision ID that should be downloaded. Ignored unless alt=media is specified.
---@field acknowledgeAbuse? boolean Whether the user is acknowledging the risk of downloading known malware or other abusive files. This is only applicable when the `alt` parameter is set to `media` and the user is the owner of the file or an organizer of the shared drive in which the file resides.
---@field fileId string The ID for the file in question.
---@field includeLabels? string A comma-separated list of IDs of labels to include in the `labelInfo` part of the response.
---@field projection? gcp.unstable.drive_v2.WatchFilesProjectionEnum|string Deprecated: This parameter has no function.

